# Day 34

## Experiment Title

Compiling and Building a Maven Project


## Objective

To understand how Maven is used to compile and build Java applications.


## Theory

Maven provides a build lifecycle that automates the process of compiling source code, testing applications, and generating executable packages. The build process ensures that all dependencies are managed properly before application execution.

Maven simplifies project compilation by automatically handling libraries and build configurations defined in the pom.xml file.


## Requirements

Java Development Kit

Apache Maven

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the command prompt inside the Maven project directory.

Verify that the project configuration is correct.

Run the Maven build process for the application.

Observe the compilation and build process.

Check the generated build files inside the target directory.


## Output

The Maven project was compiled successfully.

Build files were generated successfully inside the target directory.

The build process completed without errors.


## Result

Successfully compiled and built a Java application using Apache Maven.
